Yes indeed. There I was on the Mine Town level, and had found a co-aligned
temple (which, I may add, had been the first time I had found one co-aligned
in mine town in about 7 months, and I don't play nethack _infrequently_ you
know?)

Anyway, there I was thinking "I'm onto a good thing" and decided that I would 
put some of the cursed potions I had picked up off my previous dead body
lying at the bottom of a poinsoned, spiked pit in one of the side rooms,
and dilute them, and get them blessed (ie turn them all into holy water).

Well I waited until all the guards were out of the way and couldn't
see what I was doing, and #dip'd the potions, and eventually ran one of the
fountains out. Now what I didn't know was these damn guards are _psychic_
and immediaitly knew I had stuffed one of their fountains and got quite
nasty on me... (I guess that I was assuming that the game was smarter than
it really was -- "The guards can't see me, therefore they cant get upset
with me as they wont know I did it" -- as nethack becomes better and better
written, with more code to deal with 'real' situations it is becomming
easier to forget that the game isn't actually intelligent I find)

It wasn't long before the watch captain had got me down to a few hit points
(this was before I got my pet doggie polymorphed into a mind flayer (I
_really_ recommend mind flayers as pets, they are lethal)) so I checked the
inventory and found various itmes that might be of use, one of which was
an unidentifed harp (this was a game where I did all of the mines, and got
to about 12 level in the DoD without finding _one_ ident scroll).

I played it. Everybody got all mellow again. "There must be a god" I thought
(Amaterasu Omikami as I recall...)

It really does show that the more you play the game, the more you realise that
you should Never Say Die, there's always _something_ you can try. And theres
nothing like a lucky brush with death to make you feel a real sense of 
adventure and fulfilment while hacking.

Of course my character died later when playing by a rather nasty bones level
that another previous char of mine had created that was absolutly _crawling_
in Puddings. (Ever have a bones level that just kept coming back to haunt you?
I once lost 3 characters in the same shop...)

